    "group": "201-300",
    "title": "Search a 2D Matrix II",
    "workload": "build a 1000x1000 doubly-sorted matrix once as a flat row-major array (8MB, larger than L2), then 120000 staircase queries. A single query is only O(m+n) so the punch count is high rather than the matrix being enormous. Targets straddle the value range so roughly half hit (exiting early at varying depth) and half miss (running the full m+n staircase) -- benching only one would measure a single branch. Sink counts hits, position-weighted. NOTE: Go runs this ~4.5x faster than clang -O3 and rustc -O on IDENTICAL step counts (61709746, verified by instrumenting both); the gap persists when the matrix is shrunk to fit L2, so it is not a cache effect.",
